hw/sh4: ze0 unit flash as a CFI-02 NOR chip so FMD1: works (TODO M8.H18).

NK1's flash.dll (FMD1:) enters AMD autoselect (0x5555/0xaa, 0x2aaa/0x55,
0x5555/0x90), reads the device code at word 1 (fn 0x03d6ade8) and maps it
through its table at 0x03d625b0 (SST38VF6401 0x536b, SST39VF3201 0x235b,
S29JL032H 0x227e, S29AL032D 0x22f9, MX29LV320DB 0x22a8, M29W320EB 0x2257).
FMD_IOControl (vtable call to 0x03d6a600) refuses every IOCTL_FMD_* while
the index is 6 (fn 0x03d6b900), which is what a plain ROM gave: the
VSram and FlashManager drivers logged IOCTL_FMD_READ/ERASE errors and
Navi's OBJ_BackUp_Load failed, so the car position fell back to the
default.  An 8 MiB flash= is now a pflash_cfi02: x16, 8 x 8 KiB boot
blocks then 127 x 64 KiB (docs/hardware/unit-flash.md), id 0xbf/0x536b,
unlock 0x555/0x2aa.  Guest writes go to a temporary overlay unless
flash-rw=on.  Other sizes keep the read-only ROM of M8.C1m.  The dump is
the owner's and stays outside the repository.

Signed-off-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>


